Enhancement: lock parity Phase 4 genuine minimal-lock prune

Normal prune now uses a short exclusive claim to create a pending durable plan,
runs planning/repack/replacement-index upload under a shared append lock, then
reopens with a short exclusive lock to revalidate and delete only the durable
plan's exact candidates. `--keep-delete` leaves the ready plan for a later
revalidated cleanup; immediate prune performs both phases.

An integration test pauses phase A during replacement-index upload and proves a
backup can complete concurrently before phase B takes its exclusive deletion
lock. Unsafe recovery, dry runs, and early-index deletion retain their
established all-exclusive behavior.

